    {
      "n": 1,
      "signpost": "a greater amount",
      "definition": "used before a noun to mean a greater amount or number than before, or than another amount already mentioned",
      "explanation": "**More** goes before either a plural noun or an uncountable noun, unlike **many** and **much**, which each go with only one kind: *more books*, *more money*. It is often followed by **than**: *more time than I expected*.",
