  "synonym_discrimination": null,
  "usage_note": "**More** is the comparative form shared by both **many** and **much**: it goes with a plural countable noun or an uncountable noun alike, where those two words each go with only one kind. The superlative, shared the same way, is **most**. **More** used alone, without a following noun (*I want more*), or as an adverb before an adjective to form a comparative (*more expensive*), belongs to separate entries.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "I need more informations.",
      "correct": "I need more information.",
      "note": "**Information** is uncountable and has no plural; **more** already works with it as it is."
    }
  ],
